### Spiritual & Cultural Comfort Texts

The spiritual comfort module (`SpiritualComfort.tsx`) offers opt-in tradition-specific texts. This is one of the most sensitive areas of the project.

**Requirements for adding or modifying comfort texts:**

1. **Community review is mandatory.** Any new text representing a religious or cultural tradition must be reviewed by at least one person who identifies with that tradition and has relevant cultural knowledge. Maintainers will not merge spiritual content without this.
2. **Sources must be accurate.** Quote references (scripture, tradition) must be verifiable. Do not paraphrase sacred texts in ways that distort meaning.
3. **Reflections must be pastoral, not prescriptive.** The reflection text should hold space, not instruct. Avoid "you should", "you must", "God wants you to". Prefer "you are not alone", "there is room for this pain".
4. **No tradition is ranked.** All traditions receive the same quality and length of content. Secular/non-religious receives equal respect.
5. **Adding a new tradition:** Open a GitHub Issue first. Describe the tradition, proposed texts (in at least English), and your connection to or consultation with the community. Maintainers will coordinate review.

