## Trauma-Informed Guidelines

CalmBridge serves people in acute distress. Every contribution — code, copy, design — must be evaluated through a trauma-informed lens.

**Core principles for contributors:**

| Principle | What it means in practice |
|---|---|
| **Safety first** | Never ship a change that could reduce the visibility or effectiveness of crisis resources |
| **No pressure** | UI changes must never push or rush the user — no countdown timers on sensitive screens, no aggressive retry prompts |
| **Validation over advice** | AI prompt changes must preserve the "acknowledge before advising" structure |
| **No harmful platitudes** | Avoid "stay strong", "everything happens for a reason", "others have it worse" in any language |
| **Shame-free language** | Error messages, fallback text, and offline content must never imply fault or weakness |
| **Opt-in sensitivity** | Features like spiritual comfort must remain entirely opt-in — never assumed |

When in doubt, ask: *"Would this feel safe and respectful to someone in their worst moment?"*

